Well, I was about to write that the "skill in the single weapon
scoring the hit" referred to in the spoiler is always the primary
weapon, but I thought I'd double-check with the source, and you're
correct.

If you're two-weaponing, and you hit, then for each of your weapons
you'll get the two-weapon +DAM bonus [note: usually a penalty] for the
worse of your two-weapon skill and your skill in *that* weapon.

[For source divers, the most relevant portion is uhitm.c L899, the if
(valid_weapon_attack) block.  I did check, and the enclosing function
is called one for each weapon during two-weapon.]

So, yes, if your two-weapon skill exceeds your skill in your offhand
weapon, each level of skill in your offhand weapon type will add 1 to
your damage with every two-weapon attack.  Whether this one or two
points of damage overcomes other factors in selecting an offhand
weapon is, of course, a matter of circumstance and player preference,
but it seems David is correct that skill in offhand weapon is
(slightly) relevant to two-weapon combat in vanilla.


